<h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
<p><strong>Is contract aerosol filling legally permitted in India?</strong><br />Yes. Contract aerosol filling is legally permitted provided the filling facility holds valid licenses and operates under applicable safety, gas cylinder, and explosives regulations.</p>
<p><strong>Who carries regulatory responsibility — the brand or the contract filler?</strong><br />Responsibility is shared. The filler is responsible for safe manufacturing operations, while the brand owner is responsible for product claims, labeling accuracy, and market compliance.</p>
<p><strong>Can startups supply their own aerosol formulation?</strong><br />Yes. Startups may supply their own formulations, subject to compatibility testing, safety evaluation, and regulatory review by the filling facility.</p>
<p><strong>Are minimum order quantities mandatory?</strong><br />Yes. Minimum order quantities exist due to line setup time, material handling, quality control requirements, and regulatory compliance costs inherent to aerosol filling.</p>
<p><strong>Is export possible from contract aerosol filling plants in India?</strong><br />Yes. Export is possible provided the product, packaging, labeling, and documentation comply with destination country regulations and international transport rules.</p>

